messages:
marta: Quick note 4821 PR has mismatched examples for /v1/generate streaming. JS snippet uses camelCase in raw body and the streaming response example misses the content array which breaks parser samples.
ishan: @marta thanks. Confirming: raw HTTP examples in the API reference should use snake_case (e.g., max_new_tokens). SDK examples remain camelCase.
prashant: Yup. Backend expects snake_case in REST bodies. We should standardize all raw JSON examples to snake_case so folks copying curl/js examples don't get caught.
ryan: Also the streaming response example in the OpenAPI file only had message.role. When people copy that into SSE parser examples the code errors because message.content is undefined.
olivia: I'll update the language-specific snippets (JS, curl, python) in the page to match. Taking the JS and curl edits. Assigning to myself and will push a preview.
marta: Here's the bad snippet from the PR (copied):

```js
// from PR (incorrect for raw API)
fetch('/v1/generate', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  body: JSON.stringify({
    model: 'redwood-1',
    prompt: 'Hello',
    maxNewTokens: 64 // camelCase shown but raw API expects snake_case
  })
})
```

marta: Proposed raw-API example (use snake_case) + streaming SSE note:

```js
// raw API body (snake_case)
fetch('/v1/generate', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  body: JSON.stringify({
    model: 'redwood-1',
    prompt: 'Hello',
    max_new_tokens: 64,
    stream: true
  })
})

// SSE parsing example - include content array in each message
const es = new EventSource('/v1/generate/stream');
es.onmessage = (e) => {
  const event = JSON.parse(e.data);
  // expected shape: { message: { role: 'assistant', content: [{ type: 'output_text', text: '...' }] } }
  if (event.message && event.message.content && event.message.content[0]) {
    console.log(event.message.content[0].text);
  }
};
```

ishan: The OpenAPI examples need to be changed too  the current example in openapi/generated.yml has only role which is the root cause.
prashant: I'll open a quick patch to /openapi/generated.yml to replace the response example with a realistic content array. I can also add a tiny test to fail CI if example doesn't match our response schema.
ryan: Good call. I'll add a docs unit that loads the OpenAPI examples and validates example responses against the schema so this doesn't regress.
doc-bot: CI: docs-lint passed, preview built for branch fix-4821 -> https://staging-docs.redwood.ai/preview/4821
olivia: Pushed edits to branch and updated the deploy preview. Changed raw-JSON examples to snake_case, updated SSE/streaming response samples across JS/curl/python.
marta: Thanks. I'll add a short changelog line clarifying API vs SDK naming conventions and the streaming response shape. Closing out the coordination here.
